  "content": [
    {
      "text": "when she saw him that he was a goodly child, Ex. 2:2. If men strive, and hurt a woman with child, Ex. 21:22. If … one of them die, and have no child, Deut. 25:5 (Matt. 22:24). For this child I prayed, 1 Sam. 1:27. I am but a little child, 1 Kgs. 3:7. Divide the living child in two, 1 Kgs. 3:25. he stretched himself upon the child three times, 1 Kgs. 17:21. Train up a child in the way he should go, Prov. 22:6. Foolishness is bound in the heart of a child, Prov. 22:15. Withhold not correction from the child, Prov. 23:13. a child left to himself bringeth his mother to shame, Prov. 29:15. Woe to thee, O land, when thy king is a child, Eccl. 10:16. unto us a child is born, Isa. 9:6 (2 Ne. 19:6). a little child shall lead them, Isa. 11:6 (2 Ne. 21:6; 30:12). the child shall die an hundred years old, Isa. 65:20. she was delivered of a man child, Isa. 66:7 (Rev. 12:5). When Israel was a child, then I loved him, Hosea 11:1.",
